      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a good example of over-moderation. I will continue to voice my opinion for the exact opposite.\n\nThe world creator should not have moderation powers over normal public instances, that is what group public instances are for now. The world creator having moderation powers in all instances of their world is an old rule that has existed since long before the group features we have now, so it should just be removed. See: [remove-world-creator-moderation-powers](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/remove-world-creator-moderation-powers)\n\nIf the world creator wants to have moderation powers in an instance of their world, they should make their own group public instance. Then players will have a clear choice about if they want that moderation experience or not. Rather than the world creator being able to impose their will on any public instances of their world without giving the players a choice.\n\nIf you, as a world creator, don't want people to use your PUBLISHED world for whatever they want, you should unpublish it and make it private.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
